# Dependencies
node_modules/

# NOTE: `lib/` is intentionally NOT ignored.
#
# The compiled output is committed on purpose, and that is the one unusual
# thing about this repository layout.
#
# The alternative — gitignoring it and rebuilding from a `prepare` script at
# install time — does not survive pnpm 11. A dependency's build scripts are
# blocked until `allowBuilds` names them, and for a git-hosted dependency that
# key is the RESOLVED TARBALL URL, which embeds the commit hash. So every push
# would need a matching edit in the installing profile's pnpm-workspace.yaml,
# and anyone else installing the plugin would have to add that line themselves.
#
# Shipping the compiled output removes the build step entirely: no build script,
# no allowBuilds entry, and a git install works for anyone who clones it.
#
# The cost is that `src/` changes need `npm run build` and a commit, so the two
# can drift. `npm run verify:build` fails if they have.

# TypeScript incremental state
*.tsbuildinfo

# Packaged tarballs (`npm pack` output)
*.tgz

# Test and tool output
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Harness end-to-end scratch
.dsh-home/
e2e.out
sessions/

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

